# [[firmly|Firmly]] or [[solidly]] [[built#Adjective|built]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[Henry the Minstrel]|authorlink=Blind Harry|chapter=How Wallace Came into Scotland Again at the Battel of Elchok-Park|section=book XII|title=[[w:The Wallace|The Life and Acts of the Most Famous and Valiant Champion, Sir William Wallace, Knight of Ellerslie; Maintainer of the Liberty of Scotland. With a Preface Containing a Short Sum of the History of that Time]]|location=Edinburgh|publisher=Printed by the heirs and successors of Andrew Anderson, printer to the Queen's Most Excellent Majesty|year=1709|page=304|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=u8B0NJ3NcZkC&pg=RA10-PA4|oclc=181880224|passage=This true Man ſoon aſſembled him beforn: / Three Sons he had that '''ſtalwart''' were and bold, / And twenty Men of Kin in his Houſhold.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=George Frederick Ruxton|authorlink=George Ruxton|chapter=III|title=Life in the Far West|series=Plains and Rockies|seriesvolume=175|location=Edinburgh; London|publisher=[[w:Blackwood (publishing house)|William Blackwood and Sons]]|year=1849|page=71|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ul9ZAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA71|oclc=33260992|passage=[A] '''stalwart''' leather-clad "boy," just returned from trapping on the waters of Grand River, on the western side the mountains, who interlards his mountain jargon with Spanish words picked up in Taos and California.}}
#* {{RQ:Twain Roughing It|chapter=LVII|page=415|passage=For observe, it was an assemblage of two hundred thousand ''young'' men—not simpering, dainty, kid-gloved weaklings, but '''stalwart''', muscular, dauntless young braves, brimful of push and energy, and royally endowed with every attribute that goes to make up a peerless and magnificent manhood—the very pick and choice of the world's glorious ones.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Willa Sibert Cather|authorlink=Willa Cather|title=[[w:The Bohemian Girl (short story)|The Bohemian Girl]]|magazine=[[w:McClure's|McClure’s Magazine]]|location=[New York, N.Y.]|publisher=McClure Publications|month=August|year=1912|volume=XXXIX|number=4|section=chapter I|page=422|pageurl=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015028736356;view=1up;seq=434|oclc=19132586|passage=The driver was a '''stalwart''' woman who sat at ease in the front seat and drove her car bare-headed. She left a cloud of dust and a trail of gasoline behind her.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|writer={{w|Aaron Ehasz}}|role=Morbo|episode={{w|Crimes of the Hot}}|title={{w|Futurama}}|season=5|number=1|network={{w|Fox Broadcasting Company}}|date=10 November 2002|passage=Direct your attention now to the African turtles seen here migrating&nbsp;… Morbo wishes these '''stalwart''' nomads peace.}}
# [[courageous|Courageous]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Art II.— ''History of the Italian Language and Dialects. Saggi di Prose e Poesie de’ più celebri Scrittori d’ogni Secolo''. VI. vol. 8vo. (Selected by {{smallcaps|L. Nardini}} and {{smallcaps|S. Buonaiuti}}.) ''In Londra.'' 1798.|journal=[[w:North American Review|The North American Review]]|location=Boston, Mass.|publisher=Gray and Bowen,{{nb...|141 Washington Street}}|month=October|year=1832|volume=XXXV|issue=LXXVII|pages=301–302|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=1aZKAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA302|oclc=642444475|passage=Many other learned men of the age followed him [Romolo Amaseo] to the field, and contended with much zeal for the cause of the Latin; some even went so far as to wish the Italian completely banished entirely from the world. But '''stalwart''' champions were not wanting on the other side; and, to be brief, the impulse of public opinion soon swept away all opposition, and the popular cause was triumphant.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=E[dward] Howard|authorlink=Edward Howard (novelist)|chapter=XXXI|title=Sir Henry Morgan, the Buccaneer|location=Paris|publisher=Baudry's European Library, {{...|3, Quai Malaquais, near the Pont des Arts,}} and Stassin and Xavier,{{nb...|9, Rue du Coq [...]}}|year=1842|page=241|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=uStGAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA241|oclc=602504227|passage=Now Tomlins always acted as Morgan's major domo in tent or quarters, and was also a '''stalwart''' hand either against ox, sheep, or enemy.}}
# [[determined|Determined]]; [[staunch]].

